{#
    "I'm done with this import" (docs/features/data-import/upload.md "Finished", guided-flow.md §5.3): a plain link
    with its one sentence, at the very bottom of "Where you are" - a plain form, the confirmation is the text under
    it. Offered for an import that took rows (it can not be discarded) while nothing of it is running.
    Variables: import_id, csrf, kept_only (optional), nothing_added (optional: nothing is on the profile from this
    import - then why: `on_profile` = what it holds is on the profile already, `undone` = it was added and taken back
    and its rows are ready again, anything else = said without a reason).
#}
<form action="{{ path('data_import_done', {importId: import_id}) }}" method="post" class="mb-3" data-testid="import-finish">
    <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf }}">
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-link px-0 text-start text-wrap" style="min-height: 44px;" data-testid="import-finish-button">
        <i class="bi bi-check2-circle me-1" aria-hidden="true"></i>{{ 'data_import.finish.button'|trans }}
    </button>
    {# An import that only kept rows just for the player put nothing on the profile - the sentence does not say it did #}
    {% set nothing_keys = {on_profile: 'data_import.explain.finish_nothing', undone: 'data_import.explain.finish_undone'} %}
    <p class="fs-sm text-muted mb-0" data-testid="import-finish-explain">{{ (nothing_added|default(false) ? (nothing_keys[nothing_added] ?? 'data_import.explain.finish_none') : (kept_only|default(false) ? 'data_import.explain.finish_kept' : 'data_import.explain.finish'))|trans }}</p>
</form>
